@import copy from '../../components/copy.tscl'
@import docs from '../../layouts/docs.tscl'

<docs [title]="'Shared stores'" [path]="'/guide/stores'" [description]="'Share state between islands with stores and shared().'">
  <h1>Shared stores</h1>
  <p class="lead">Put state that several islands use in a store: a module that exports <code>state()</code> values. Each island takes a local name for it with <code>shared()</code> and reads and writes it like its own state.</p>
  <div class="sample"><pre><code verbatim>// stores/cart.ts
import { state } from 'clarusjs/runtime'
export const cart = state([])

// components/cart-count.tscl
<script>
  import { cart } from '../stores/cart.ts'
  let items = shared(cart)
</script>
<span>{{ items.length }} in cart</span></code></pre><copy attach="interaction" /></div>
  <p>On the server, a shared value is rendered from the store's initial value, never its current one, and each render gets its own copy: a server keeps modules alive across requests, so anything else could show one visitor's data to another. Store values must therefore be plain data that can be copied.</p>
</docs>
